      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Prospectors flocked to Belt Creek in the 1860s, founding mining camp Canyon City, later renamed Neihart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neihart%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Neihart sits atop Precambrian rocks rich in gold, lead, sapphires, silver, and zinc.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neihart%2C_Montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Neihart lies in the heart of the Little Belt Mountains, surrounded by Lewis and Clark National Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neihart%2C_Montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 89, the Kings Hill Scenic Byway, winds through Neihart’s rugged highlands, providing panoramic views of the surrounding mountains.",
